git commit -m "Static-on-Netlify migration, Phase 1 (additive). Reorganize: Netlify/ -> Landing/ for clarity; new Tools/ holds a copy of the static surfaces (index + shared.css/js + pivot-cup/ + riser-pad/) for a new Netlify site at tools.longboardtechnology.com. Render/site/ stays in place during the DNS migration window so the existing CNAME keeps serving valid pages until Netlify takes over; Phase 2 will strip it. Tools/_redirects proxies /api/* -> https://lt-tools.onrender.com/api/:splat (status 200 = transparent proxy, keeps requests same-origin so no CORS plumbing). Loading-overlay extended with an optional sub-line: shared.js setLoading(on, msg, submsg); both generator pages add an empty <div id='loading-sub'> inside the overlay and pass a 'First preview can take ~30 seconds while the server starts up.' hint on the first call only (flag flips on first successful response). New shared.js helper LT.pingApi fires fire-and-forget GET to https://lt-tools.onrender.com/api/health on every tool-page DOMContentLoaded so direct visitors warm Render the same way Landing-page visitors already do. Cleanup: removes 4 Google Drive sync-conflict (1).html/.css files that had been tracked in git."
